# Metadata for TriX (Triples-in-XML) test files

These are RDF datasets serialized in the TriX (Triples in XML) syntax
(namespace http://www.w3.org/2004/03/trix/trix-1/). They are collected from
external RDF library test suites: four from RDFLib and one from Ruby-RDF.
They exercise the graphinout RDF reader against TriX named graphs, plain and
typed literals, blank-node ids and edge cases.

ddot.it/this ..kind.. collected
ddot.it/this ..format.. format:trix
ddot.it/this ..content.. TriX (Triples-in-XML) example datasets collected from the RDFLib and Ruby-RDF test suites.


# --- File: rdflib-aperture.trix ---

rdflib-aperture.trix ..kind.. collected
rdflib-aperture.trix ..format.. format:trix
rdflib-aperture.trix ..content.. TriX document with a single named <graph> (uri file:/home/grimnes/tmp/aperture/) holding triples generated by the Aperture semantic-desktop crawler over a local file tree. Uses <uri>, <plainLiteral> and <typedLiteral datatype="...XMLSchema#dateTime"> objects describing files via the Aperture data ontology.
rdflib-aperture.trix ..tests.. TriX parsing of a named graph with mixed object kinds: <uri>, <plainLiteral> and xsd:dateTime <typedLiteral>.
rdflib-aperture.trix ..source url.. https://github.com/RDFLib/rdflib
rdflib-aperture.trix ..license.. BSD-3-Clause


# --- File: rdflib-bnode-context.trix ---

rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..kind.. collected
rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..format.. format:trix
rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..content.. TriX document with two <graph> elements, each identified by an <id> (blank-node / graph identifier) and containing one triple whose subject is also an <id>. Objects are <plainLiteral> values (Michele, Kevin) with foaf:Friend predicate. Lowercase <trix> root element variant.
rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..tests.. TriX blank-node (<id>) handling as graph names and triple subjects across multiple named graphs (bnode context).
rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..source url.. https://github.com/RDFLib/rdflib
rdflib-bnode-context.trix ..license.. BSD-3-Clause


# --- File: rdflib-example.trix ---

rdflib-example.trix ..kind.. collected
rdflib-example.trix ..format.. format:trix
rdflib-example.trix ..content.. TriX document with a named <graph> (uri http://bibliographica.org/entity/E10008) describing a bibliographic FOAF Document/Agent: rdf:type, foaf:primaryTopic, foaf:name etc. Lowercase <trix> root element. A general-purpose TriX example.
rdflib-example.trix ..tests.. TriX parsing of a typical named graph with <uri> and <plainLiteral> objects and FOAF/rdf:type predicates.
rdflib-example.trix ..source url.. https://github.com/RDFLib/rdflib
rdflib-example.trix ..license.. BSD-3-Clause


# --- File: rdflib-jena-01.trix ---

rdflib-jena-01.trix ..kind.. collected
rdflib-jena-01.trix ..format.. format:trix
rdflib-jena-01.trix ..content.. Minimal/degenerate TriX document: an empty <TriX> root element with no <graph> content, declared with XML version 1.1. A Jena-compatibility variant used as an empty-document edge case.
rdflib-jena-01.trix ..tests.. TriX parsing of an empty document (no graphs/triples) and XML 1.1 declaration handling (Jena compatibility).
rdflib-jena-01.trix ..source url.. https://github.com/RDFLib/rdflib
rdflib-jena-01.trix ..license.. BSD-3-Clause


# --- File: ruby-rdf-examples.trix ---

ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..kind.. collected
ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..format.. format:trix
ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..content.. TriX example from Ruby-RDF: a default (unnamed) <graph> with triples about example.org/Bob and example.org/Mary using <uri>, <plainLiteral> and xsd:integer <typedLiteral> objects. Includes an XML comment showing the equivalent N-Triples form.
ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..tests.. TriX parsing of a default graph with <uri>, <plainLiteral> and xsd:integer <typedLiteral> objects.
ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..source url.. https://github.com/ruby-rdf/rdf-trix
ruby-rdf-examples.trix ..license.. Public Domain (Unlicense)
